SUMMARY:Raleigh Wide Open
DESCRIPTION:We are getting excited for Raleigh Wide Open!\nThe Music Festival will take over Fayetteville Street\, including the museum! \nWe will be hosting interviews and book events on Friday\, Oct. 2\, and Saturday\, Oct. 3. We hope to see you there! \nSaturday\, Oct. 3 – Book Events\n\nDavid Menconi “Step It Up and Go”\, 2 – 2:30 p.m.\nAlice Gerrard “Custom Made Woman”\, 2:30 – 3 p.m.\nPhil Jamison “Hoedowns\, Reels & Frolics”\, 3 – 3:30 p.m.\nEddie Huffman “Doc Watson: A Life in Music”\, 3:30 – 4 p.m.\n\nLocation: City of Raleigh Museum\nAges: All
URL:https://nchumanities.org/event/raleigh-wide-open-2/
LOCATION:City of Raleigh Museum\, 220 Fayetteville Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27601\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://nchumanities.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/raleigh-wide-1.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="The City of Raleigh Museum":MAILTO:cormuseum@gmail.com
GEO:35.7776508;-78.6397629
