SUMMARY:"Music of the New Nation" Concert at Mordecai
DESCRIPTION:Bring thyself hither to Mordecai Historic Park for a Grand Concert of Vocal and Instrumental Music with the band Ampersand!\nAmpersand’s special Revolutionary War-era program\, “Music of the New Nation”\, focuses on the experience of the home front and everyday people as they faced the battle for independence. \nThis trio of musicians brings guitar\, mandolin\, bouzouki\, hammered dulcimer\, cello\, and penny whistles to underscore rich vocal harmonies and great joy in sharing this traditional music with modern audiences. The concert will take place in St. Mark’s Chapel on the grounds of Mordecai Historic Park. For more information\, call 919-996-4364.
URL:https://nchumanities.org/event/music-of-the-new-nation-concert-at-mordecai/
LOCATION:Mordecai Historic Park\, 1 Mimosa Street\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27604\, United States
CATEGORIES:Humanities Sector Event
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://nchumanities.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Trio-by-brick-wall.jpg
END:VEVENT
